                "kind": "TapSelf"
              }
            ],
            "do": {
              "kind": "Unsupported",
              "reason": "\u0022An opponent was dealt 7 or more damage this turn\u0022 cannot be said. The amount is DamageDealtThisTurn, whose To must name a player to act on, and AnOpponent - the only reference that means \u0022some opponent\u0022 - is refused there (L041). EachOpponent would read \u0022every opponent\u0022, which is a different card in a multiplayer game, and ChoosePlayer or TargetPlayer would invent a choice the card does not print. No Condition asks how much damage a player was dealt this turn, so the gate on the play permission has no spelling and the MayPlay cannot be written without it.",
              "text": "You may play the exiled card without paying its mana cost if an opponent was dealt 7 or more damage this turn."
            },
            "timing": "Any",
            "where": "Battlefield",
            "anyPlayerMayActivate": false,
            "text": "{R}, {T}: You may play the exiled card without paying its mana cost if an opponent was dealt 7 or more damage this turn."
          }
        ],
